  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:102586",
  "description": "The golang packages provide the Go programming language compiler.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * cmd/go: golang: cmd/go: arbitrary command execution via untrusted GCC spec files (CVE-2026-97034)\n  * cmd/go: cmd/compile: golang: golang: arbitrary code execution via crafted cgo compiler directives (CVE-2026-97043)\n  * cmd/go: golang: cmd/go: arbitrary code execution via crafted cgo directives (CVE-2026-97035)\n  * net/[http](http): golang: net/[http](http): Denial of Service via race condition when handling oversized HTTP/1 requests (CVE-2026-97054)\n  * cmd/go: golang: cmd/go: Arbitrary code execution via unsafe cgo compiler and linker flags (CVE-2026-97033)\n  * cmd/compile: cmd/link: golang: golang: Arbitrary code execution via external linker flag injection (CVE-2026-97041)\n  * cmd/go: cmd/link: golang: golang: Arbitrary code execution via crafted .syso files (CVE-2026-97040)\n  * cmd/go: golang: cmd/go: arbitrary code execution via malicious cgo linker flags (CVE-2026-97037)\n  * cmd/go: golang: cmd/go: arbitrary code execution via crafted cgo linker flags (CVE-2026-97036)\n  * cmd/go: golang: cmd/go: Arbitrary code execution via crafted linker inputs (CVE-2026-97038)\n  * cmd/go: golang: cmd/go: arbitrary code execution via crafted pkg-config directives (CVE-2026-97039)\n  * cmd/cgo: cmd/compile: cmd/link: golang: Go: Arbitrary code execution via unsafe linker arguments on Windows (CVE-2026-97042)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * Update Go to version 1.27.4+1 [rhel-9.9] (JIRA:RHEL-311805)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
  "fromstr": "packager@almalinux.org",
